. 
. * ============================
. * Data Preparation * 
. * ============================
. 
. * LOAD AND MERGE DATA * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         use "$IN/ppathl.dta", clear // use ppathl as a starting dataset
(SOEP-Core, v37 (EU Edition), doi:10.5684/soep.core.v37eu)

. 
.         * Merge ppathl with all datasets, that you deem relevant for your ana
> lysis. (Tip: use keepusing() to specify which variables to keep from the usin
> g dataset; the default is all.)
. 
.         * biobirth contains information on fertility history
.         merge m:1 pid using "$IN/biobirth.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable pid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable cid was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(variable gebjahr was int, now double to accommodate using data's values)
(label sex already defined)
(label sex_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pgen contains user-friendly data on the individual level that are c
> onsolidated from different sources
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable syear was long, now double to accommodate using data's values)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * pl contains all variables from the individual questionnaire
.         merge 1:1 pid syear using "$IN/pl.dta", nogen keep(master matches)
(variable inputdataset was str6, now str9 to accommodate using data's values)
(label cid already defined)
(label pid_EN already defined)
(label cid_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

.         * hgen contains generated variables on household level from the house
> hold interview; use for household net income
.         merge m:1 hid syear using "$IN/hgen.dta", nogen keep(master matches) 
> keepusing(hid syear hghinc)
(label iyear already defined)
(label iyear_EN already defined)

    Result                      Number of obs
    -----------------------------------------
    Not matched                             0
    Matched                            35,228  
    -----------------------------------------

. 
.         label language EN // change language of the labels to English

. 
.         *save "$DATA/h3_dataset.dta", replace // save merged dataset
. 
. 
. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. * FILTERS * (Please adapt according to your needs)
.  
.         * Example: only keep participants from private households
.         *keep if inlist(pop,1,2)
. 
. 
. * GENERATE VARIABLES * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         set seed 123

. 
.         * Indicator that respondent has only one biological child:
.         generate have_one_child = biokids==1

.         
.         * Indicator that first biological child is a daughter:
.         generate d_daughter = .
(35,228 missing values generated)

.         replace d_daughter = 1 if kidsex01==2   
(11,310 real changes made)

.         replace d_daughter = 0 if kidsex01==1
(13,281 real changes made)

.         
.         * Employed full time indicator based on plb0022_h
.         generate employed_ft_v1 = .
(35,228 missing values generated)

.         replace employed_ft_v1 = 1 if plb0022_h==1
(10,064 real changes made)

.         replace employed_ft_v1 = 0 if plb0022_h>=2 & plb0022_h<=12
(17,042 real changes made)

.         
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         
.         * Test 2 H3: 
.         * If we assume that a mother being empoyed full time (employed_ft_v1)
>  is a good measure of gender equality in the household.
.         * Then, accordingly, we run a linear OLS regression analysis with emp
> loyed_ft_v1 as dependent variable and the dummy variable d_daughter as indepe
> ndent variable.
.         * We restrict the sample to mothers and individuals with valid answer
> s to the variables included in the regression
.         
.         local i=1  // test number within hypothesis

.         local outcome`i' = "employed_ft_v1"

.         
.         regress `outcome`i'' i.d_daughter c.bioage##c.bioage hghinc pgisced97
>  i.syear if sex==2 & have_one_child==1 & (hghinc>0 & hghinc!=.) & (pgisced97>
> =0 & pgisced97!=.), vce(robust)

